Student Performance Analysis Using R

Project Overview

This project analyzes student performance data using R programming and beginner-friendly data science techniques.

The main objective is to identify patterns and relationships between student-related factors and academic performance and to develop a simple model for predicting student scores.

Objectives

- Import and understand student performance data.
- Clean and preprocess the dataset.
- Perform Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA).
- Create meaningful data visualizations.
- Analyze relationships between variables.
- Build a basic Linear Regression model.
- Evaluate model performance.
- Prepare a reproducible final report.

Technologies Used

- R
- RStudio
- R Markdown
- tidyverse
- dplyr
- ggplot2
- readr
- Linear Regression
- Git and GitHub

